@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-withdrawal`

-- g5-tests-withdrawal.l4: tests of g5-withdrawal.l4 (ss.39 and 40).
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.39 and 40 (inputs/law.wiki lines 324 to 337) BEFORE any of
-- this was run.  A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so the rules are exercised with #TRACE, each with its
-- expected result written above it as `-- EXPECT:` and checked by work/g5/tracecheck.py.
-- The calendars of rest days below are illustrations for the tests and say nothing about any calendar.

§ `Tests of ss 39 and 40`

§§ `Fixtures`

`30 days` MEANS `a number of days fixed by the Minister` 30
`14 days` MEANS `a number of days fixed by the Minister` 14
`1 month` MEANS `a number of months fixed by the Minister` 1
`1 year` MEANS `a number of years fixed by the Minister` 1
`until 10 March 2026` MEANS `a last day fixed by the Minister` (YMD 2026 3 10)

-- Demand: made on, the time directed
`a demand of 2 March 2026 for 14 days`  MEANS `Demand under section 39(b)` OF (YMD 2026 3 2),  `14 days`
`a demand of 31 January 2026 for 1 month` MEANS `Demand under section 39(b)` OF (YMD 2026 1 31), `1 month`
`a demand of 2 March 2026 until 10 March 2026` MEANS `Demand under section 39(b)` OF (YMD 2026 3 2), `until 10 March 2026`

`a calendar with Monday 16 March 2026 a rest day` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 3 16)
`a calendar with 31 January 2026 a rest day` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 1 31)
`a calendar with no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (EMPTY)

-- Case: hearing, (1) false information, (2) condition lapsed, (3) breach, (4) special circumstances, (5) poor level,
-- the demand (if any), met in time, compliance impossible
--                                                                     hearing  (1)    (2)    (3)    (4)    (5)    demand                                             met    impossible
`false information, heard`                      MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE,   TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING,                                           FALSE, FALSE
`false information, no hearing`                 MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF FALSE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING,                                           FALSE, FALSE
`special circumstances, heard`                  MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE,   FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, NOTHING,                                           FALSE, FALSE
`poor professional level, heard`                MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE,   FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  NOTHING,                                           FALSE, FALSE
`no ground, heard`                              MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE,   FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING,                                           FALSE, FALSE
`a lapsed condition, no demand`                 MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE,   FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING,                                           FALSE, FALSE
`a breach, no demand`                           MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE,   FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING,                                           FALSE, FALSE
`a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (JUST `a demand of 2 March 2026 for 14 days`), FALSE, FALSE
`a breach, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met`           MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, (JUST `a demand of 2 March 2026 for 14 days`), FALSE, FALSE
`a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, met in time` MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (JUST `a demand of 2 March 2026 for 14 days`), TRUE,  FALSE
`a lapsed condition that cannot be restored, no demand`      MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE
`a lapsed condition and a poor professional level, no demand` MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE
`a lapsed condition that cannot be restored, no hearing`     MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE
`a lapsed condition, demand of 31 January for 1 month, not met` MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (JUST `a demand of 31 January 2026 for 1 month`), FALSE, FALSE
`a lapsed condition, demand until 10 March, not met` MEANS `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (JUST `a demand of 2 March 2026 until 10 March 2026`), FALSE, FALSE

§§ `s 39 -- Revocation or suspension`

-- s.39(a) (src:325-330): after a written hearing, on one of five grounds.
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `false information, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `special circumstances, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `poor professional level, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `false information, no hearing` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `no ground, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`

-- s.39(b) (src:331): a lapsed condition or a breach, (a)(2) or (3), needs a demand first, a decision after its time
-- ran out, and no compliance; or impossibility.  No demand: no revocation.
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a breach, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
-- Demand of 2 March for 14 days: s.10(a) puts the last day on 16 March (2 March is not counted).  The person has
-- that whole day, so the Minister may act only from 17 March.
#ASSERT `s 39(b) — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` `a demand of 2 March 2026 for 14 days` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 16
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 9) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 16) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 17) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 6 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a breach, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 16) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a breach, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 17) `a calendar with no rest days`
-- A demand met in time ends the matter, whenever the Minister looks.
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, met in time` (YMD 2026 3 17) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, met in time` (YMD 2026 9 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
-- Impossibility needs no demand; the hearing is still needed.
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition that cannot be restored, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition that cannot be restored, no hearing` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
-- (b) bars only revocation "under (a)(2) or (3)": a person also at a poor professional level can be reached under (a)(5).
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition and a poor professional level, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`

-- Fork F-P25 (kind D): the last day of the time directed is counted with s.10(c) when it is a rest day.  Monday
-- 16 March 2026 a rest day moves the last day to 17 March, so the Minister may act from 18 March; without s.10(c),
-- from 17 March.
#ASSERT `s 39(b), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` `a demand of 2 March 2026 for 14 days` `a calendar with Monday 16 March 2026 a rest day` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 17
#ASSERT `s 39(b), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` `a demand of 2 March 2026 for 14 days` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 16
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 17) `a calendar with Monday 16 March 2026 a rest day`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 18) `a calendar with Monday 16 March 2026 a rest day`
#ASSERT `s 39, s 10(c) not applied — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 17)
#ASSERT NOT `s 39, s 10(c) not applied — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 16)
#ASSERT `s 39, s 10(c) not applied — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `false information, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 39, s 10(c) not applied — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `false information, no hearing` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 39, s 10(c) not applied — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 39, s 10(c) not applied — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition that cannot be restored, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- A month from 31 January ends on 28 February (s.10(b)); a stated last day is a date and s.10(c) leaves it.
#ASSERT `s 39(b) — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` `a demand of 31 January 2026 for 1 month` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 31 January for 1 month, not met` (YMD 2026 2 28) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 31 January for 1 month, not met` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39(b), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` `a demand of 31 January 2026 for 1 month` `a calendar with 31 January 2026 a rest day` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 39(b) — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` `a demand of 2 March 2026 until 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `s 39(b), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` `a demand of 2 March 2026 until 10 March 2026` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand until 10 March, not met` (YMD 2026 3 10) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand until 10 March, not met` (YMD 2026 3 11) `a calendar with no rest days`

-- Acts for the traces.
`the suspension for 30 days` MEANS `suspend the authorisation of a tester or an expert for a period` `30 days`

-- s.39(a) (src:325): the power to revoke, and to suspend for a period.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 39(a) — the Minister may revoke the authorisation of a tester or expert` `false information, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 39(a) — the Minister may revoke the authorisation of a tester or expert` `false information, no hearing` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 39(a) — the Minister may revoke the authorisation of a tester or expert` `a lapsed condition, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 39(a) — the Minister may suspend the authorisation of a tester or expert for a period he sets` `special circumstances, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the suspension for 30 days` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 39(a) — the Minister may suspend the authorisation of a tester or expert for a period he sets` `a breach, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the suspension for 30 days` AT 2
-- s.39(b) as a prohibition: revoking on a ground it governs, before it is satisfied, is a breach by the Minister.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 39(b) — the Minister shall not revoke the authorisation on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached before the cure-first rule is satisfied` `a lapsed condition, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 39(b) — the Minister shall not revoke the authorisation on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached before the cure-first rule is satisfied` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 16) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 39(b) — the Minister shall not revoke the authorisation on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached before the cure-first rule is satisfied` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 17) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 39(b) — the Minister shall not revoke the authorisation on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached before the cure-first rule is satisfied` `a lapsed condition and a poor professional level, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 39(b) — the Minister shall not revoke the authorisation on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached before the cure-first rule is satisfied` `false information, heard` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 39(b) — the Minister shall not revoke the authorisation on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached before the cure-first rule is satisfied` `a lapsed condition that cannot be restored, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert` AT 2

§§§ `s 39(a) -- the period of a suspension (P24)`

-- The suspension began on Thursday 2026-01-01.  30 days from it end on 2026-01-31 (s.10(a)); the first day and the
-- last are days of the suspension, the day before and the day after are not.
`a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`  MEANS `Suspension under section 39(a)` OF (YMD 2026 1 1),   `30 days`
`a suspension of 1 month from 31 January 2025` MEANS `Suspension under section 39(a)` OF (YMD 2025 1 31),  `1 month`
`a suspension of 1 year from 29 February 2024` MEANS `Suspension under section 39(a)` OF (YMD 2024 2 29),  `1 year`
`a suspension until 15 March 2026`             MEANS `Suspension under section 39(a)` OF (YMD 2026 1 1),   (`a last day fixed by the Minister` (YMD 2026 3 15))
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension of 1 month from 31 January 2025` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension of 1 year from 29 February 2024` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension until 15 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 1 31) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2025 2 28) `by` `a suspension of 1 month from 31 January 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2025 3 1) `by` `a suspension of 1 month from 31 January 2025`
-- Fork F-P24 (kind V, s.10(c) not applied): with 31 January a rest day the suspension still ends on 31 January;
-- the alternative moves its last day to 1 February.
#ASSERT `s 39(a), s 10(c) applied — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026` `a calendar with 31 January 2026 a rest day` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT `s 39(a), s 10(c) applied — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 39(a), s 10(c) applied — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension until 15 March 2026` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15

§§§ `s 36(e) and s 39 -- when an authorisation is in force`

-- Authorisation: given on, last day of the period fixed in the instrument, revoked on, suspensions
--                                                               given               last day             revoked                suspensions
`an authorisation for 2026, never withdrawn`  MEANS `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31), NOTHING,                (EMPTY)
`an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026`    MEANS `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31), (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)), (EMPTY)
`an authorisation suspended in January`       MEANS `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31), NOTHING,                (LIST `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`)
`an authorisation with two suspensions`       MEANS `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31), NOTHING,                (LIST `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`, `a suspension until 15 March 2026`)
`an authorisation suspended and later revoked` MEANS `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31), (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)), (LIST `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`)
-- Both edges of the instrument's period.
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `an authorisation for 2026, never withdrawn`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 12 31) `an authorisation for 2026, never withdrawn`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `an authorisation for 2026, never withdrawn`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `an authorisation for 2026, never withdrawn`
-- Revocation ends it from the day of the revocation.
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 14) `an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 15) `an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 16) `an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026`
-- Suspension takes out its days only.
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `an authorisation suspended in January`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 1 31) `an authorisation suspended in January`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `an authorisation suspended in January`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 12 31) `an authorisation suspended in January`
-- Two suspensions, both beginning on 1 January: the first to 31 January, the second to 15 March, so the authorisation
-- is out of force until 15 March and in force again from 16 March.
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `an authorisation with two suspensions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 3 15) `an authorisation with two suspensions`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 3 16) `an authorisation with two suspensions`
-- A suspended authorisation that is later revoked: out in January, in until the revocation, out from it.
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 14) `an authorisation suspended and later revoked`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 15) `an authorisation suspended and later revoked`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 1 15) `an authorisation suspended and later revoked`

§§ `s 40 -- Application of laws`

-- s.40 (src:334-337): testers and experts have the status of State employees for three enactments, and for no
-- other; nobody else is equated by it.
#ASSERT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `a tester` `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`
#ASSERT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `a tester` `the provisions of the Penal Law about public servants`
#ASSERT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `a tester` `the Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969`
#ASSERT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `an expert` `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`
#ASSERT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `an expert` `the provisions of the Penal Law about public servants`
#ASSERT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `an expert` `the Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969`
#ASSERT NOT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `a tester` `any other enactment than the three listed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `an expert` `any other enactment than the three listed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `a testing body` `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`
#ASSERT NOT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `a person` `the provisions of the Penal Law about public servants`
#ASSERT NOT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `an inspector` `the Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969`
#ASSERT NOT `s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` `the senior inspector` `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`

-- Fork F-START and F-STATUS-DAY: on the alternative a suspension begins the day after the one it began on, and a
-- revocation takes effect the day after it is made.
#ASSERT NOT `s 39(a), beginning the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 39(a), beginning the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 1 2) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 39(a), beginning the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 1 31) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39(a), beginning the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after it is made — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 15) `an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after it is made — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 16) `an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after it is made — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `an authorisation suspended in January`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), s 39, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after it is made — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 1 2) `an authorisation suspended in January`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after it is made — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `an authorisation suspended in January`

-- Fork F-GROUNDS: a lapsed condition AND a poor professional level, no demand.  The reading taken reaches him under
-- (a)(5), which (b) does not touch; the stricter reading applies the cure-first rule because (a)(2) is also present.
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition and a poor professional level, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 39, the cure-first rule applying whenever (a)(2) or (3) exists — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition and a poor professional level, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
